#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:525
msgid ""
"This is generally not used in the manual, and should only be used where it "
"is absolutely required to represent content that needs exact formatting, but "
"never merely for aesthetic reasons."
msgstr ""
"Ogólnie, nie używamy tego w podręczniku i powinno to być używane tylko, gdy "
"jest to bezwzględnie wymagane do przedstawienia treści, która wymaga "
"dokładnego formatowania, lecz nigdy tylko z powodów estetycznych."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:530
msgid "Glossaries, Terms and Index"
msgstr "Słowniki, pojęcia, spis treści"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:532
msgid "These are sphinx features."
msgstr "To są możliwości sfinksa."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:534
msgid ""
"Index is used in the top section, right now only single index entries are "
"used."
msgstr ""
"Spis jest używany w górnym obszarze. Obecnie używane są tylko pojedyncze "
"wpisy."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:536
msgid ""
"Glossaries are used for some of the menu entry sections, but not all of them."
msgstr ""
"Słowniki są używane dla niektórych wpisów menu, lecz nie do wszystkich z "
"nich."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:539
msgid "Quotes"
msgstr "Cudzysłowy"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:541
msgid "Quotes are done like this::"
msgstr "Cytaty tworzy się następująco::"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:543
msgid ""
"I am not sure why you'd need quotes in a user manual...\n"
"\n"
"-- Wolthera"
msgstr ""
"Nie jestem pewny po co ci cytowania w podręczniku użytkownika...\n"
"\n"
"-- Wolthera"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:547
msgid "This becomes a blockquote."
msgstr "To staje się blockquote."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:549
msgid "I am not sure why you'd need quotes in a user manual..."
msgstr "Nie jestem pewien po co ci cudzysłowy w podręczniku użytkownika..."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:553
msgid ""
"We do actually use quotes in some places. Try to add a link to the name to "
"define where it came from."
msgstr ""
"W niektórych miejscach używamy cudzysłowów. Spróbuj dodać odnośnik do nazwy, "
"aby wskazać skąd ona pochodzi."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:554
msgid "Wolthera"
msgstr "Wolthera"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:556
msgid "Text for Non-English Translations Only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:558
msgid ""
"You can use the following to include text that only makes sense for non-"
"English translations of the manual, for example to provide non-English "
"readers with the English names of an item for reference::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:562
msgid ""
".. only:: non_english\n"
"\n"
"    This content is hidden for the English version, but translatable and\n"
"    shows up in non-English versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:568
msgid "Notes for Translators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:570
msgid ""
"If you are translating the manual for a language that does not usually use "
"whitespaces around words (e.g. Chinese and Japanese), you can use an escaped "
"whitespace to separate markup and words. This is particularly useful for "
"page links, like this::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:575
msgid "床前\\ `明月 <https://krita.org/>`_\\ 光"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:577
msgid ""
"Note that when translating from a PO file, you should escape the backslash "
"with another backslash::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:580
msgid "床前\\\\ `明月 <https://krita.org/>`_\\\\ 光"
msgstr ""

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_conventions.rst:582
msgid ""
"The above produces \"床前\\ `明月 <https://krita.org/>`_\\ 光\", instead of "
"\"床前 `明月 <https://krita.org/>`_ 光\"."
msgstr ""

#~ msgid "We don't actually use this anywhere in the manual."
#~ msgstr "Nie używamy tego nigdzie w podręczniku."
